1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,640
Behind the Order.

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:09,450
In this simulation, you are a public health law and ethics analyst at a county health department.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,630
A computer system called ComplianceWatch predicts which patients might stop following their treatment orders.

4
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:27,540
It has flagged Mr Tunde Balogun, who is being treated for tuberculosis, as eighty-eight percent high risk.

5
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,710
A hearing is five days away.

6
00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:37,440
Your recommendation could mean more support for him, or a court petition to detain him.

7
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:41,250
It is a decision about a person's freedom.

8
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:45,030
But a risk score is not proof.

9
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:48,680
It cannot tell you why something happened.

10
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:56,620
Your job is to look behind the number, check the evidence, and decide what it really shows.

11
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:02,710
You will do this work in the Compliance Sandbox, on this computer.

12
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,450
Start with the queue of flagged cases.

13
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:09,790
Select a case to open its record.

14
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,580
Read the whole record, not just the score.

15
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,330
Every detail can change the picture.

16
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:19,910
Each task asks for a judgement.

17
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:26,780
You will sort evidence, link records, weigh trade-offs and make a recommendation.

18
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:31,740
Drag items into place, or select them and choose.

19
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,570
Your work saves as a draft.

20
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:39,720
When you confirm, the decision is locked.

21
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,130
Everything you record goes into the case file.

22
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:51,210
Other people may rely on it later, so write down why you decided, not just what.

23
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,370
You can minimise or close the app at any time.

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,440
Your work is saved.

25
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:01,280
There is no single right score.

26
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:05,990
Think it through, explain your reasoning, and let's begin.
